precept FeeSchedule

# A stateless data-only precept governing a single fee schedule for a service
# or product line. A fee schedule holds the base price, the allowed discount
# lever, the minimum chargeable amount, and the tax rate that applies —
# together they determine what the host application bills.
#
# Pricing levers (BaseFee, DiscountPercent, MinimumCharge) are editable — the
# host's pricing UI adjusts them. TaxRate and CurrencyCode are intentionally
# locked: they are jurisdiction-level settings that must go through a separate
# administrative approval flow, not direct editing on a fee record.

field CurrencyCode as currency default 'USD'

field BaseFee as money in '{CurrencyCode}' default '0 {CurrencyCode}' nonnegative editable
field DiscountPercent as decimal default 0 nonnegative max 100 maxplaces 2 editable
field MinimumCharge as money in '{CurrencyCode}' default '0 {CurrencyCode}' nonnegative editable
field TaxRate as decimal default 0.1 nonnegative max 1 maxplaces 4

rule MinimumCharge <= BaseFee because "Minimum charge {MinimumCharge} exceeds the base fee {BaseFee} — the minimum cannot raise a quote above the headline price"
